<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valmiera</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wolmar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valmiera (German: Wolmar) is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauja">Gauja</a> river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidzeme">Vidzeme</a>, northern Latvia. It grew around a castle of the Livonian Order founded in 1283, became a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a> and was a frequent meeting place of the Livonian Landtag. It was repeatedly fought over in the wars between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valmiera.jpg" alt="Valmiera" width="320" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nikolay Yagunov / Николай Ягунов · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:44_%D0%9B%D0%B0_%D0%92%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%BC%D0%B8%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B0.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
